const OPENING_ADVENTURES = "# A Light at Reedbank — Opening Adventures\n\nOriginal fantasy dialogue. Scripture remains in scripture.md, unchanged. These optional conversations never gate travel.\n\n## reedbank-aunt · Aunt Nessa · The wick and the road\n\nNessa ties a fresh wick with blue thread. “For the wayfarers’ lantern. Their camp is beside Woodland Road; keep the water on your left until the road bends east.” Outside, a fiddle is trying to keep pace with three laughing children.\n\n“The Book’s open by the door if you want a passage for the road. Take your time. There will still be oatcakes when you get back.”\n\n#### Success\n\nShe tucks the wick into your satchel. “Nothing grand. Just a kindness somebody needs.” The south door opens onto the landing; the boardwalk joins the eastern bank path.\n\n#### Short\n\n“A wick for the elven wayfarers. South door, then east along the bank. Oatcakes when you return.”\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"reedbank-aunt\",\n  \"kind\": \"npc\",\n  \"region\": \"riverbank\",\n  \"enemy\": \"girl\",\n  \"locations\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": [\n        34,\n        30.9\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"repeatable\": true,\n  \"accept\": [],\n  \"speech\": \"\\u201cA wick for the elven wayfarers. South door, then east along the bank. Oatcakes when you return.\\u201d\",\n  \"grants\": []\n}\n```\n\n## reedbank-festival · Tobin · A festival worth lingering over\n\nTobin balances a tray of honey cakes beside the bunting. “You’re off already? The boat race hasn’t started!” A cheer travels along the docks; somebody has launched a very determined washbasin.\n\n“You can walk to the elves. Follow the boards east, then take the bank path uphill. No swimming required.”\n\n#### Success\n\nHe sets aside a cake. “For the walk home. If I don’t eat it first.” Across the river, lanterns swing over a second gathering. The village is wider than this one landing.\n\n#### Short\n\n“Follow the boards east, then the bank path uphill. I’ll save a cake. Probably.”\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"reedbank-festival\",\n  \"kind\": \"npc\",\n  \"region\": \"riverbank\",\n  \"enemy\": \"boy\",\n  \"locations\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": [\n        62.6,\n        55.9\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"repeatable\": true,\n  \"accept\": [],\n  \"speech\": \"\\u201cFollow the boards east, then the bank path uphill. I\\u2019ll save a cake. Probably.\\u201d\",\n  \"grants\": []\n}\n```\n\n## woodland-elven-wayfarer · Maerin · Beyond the bend\n\nYou hear a kettle before you see the camp. Two travelers have hung their cloaks between the birches; a small lantern waits beside a coil of rope. The taller elf looks up from mending a boot.\n\n“A Reedbank wick! Nessa remembers everything.” Maerin smiles. “I tried to repair ours with the wrong kind of rush. Being old is no protection against being foolish.”\n\n#### Success\n\n“We’re all creatures of Christ, the Maker of these woods. Whatever wisdom we have is received.” He settles the new wick into the lantern. “The Book is worth knowing on a quiet day, too. Remembered words can help us act with courage; a stumble in remembering does not tell us the strength of somebody’s faith.”\n\nFarther east, a bell sounds through the trees. “That is Greenwood. The festival folk there have an errand for a willing traveler. Follow the golden road. Or sit with us a while.”\n\n#### Short\n\n“Thank you for the wick! Greenwood lies east. We’re fellow creatures under Christ, and glad of a neighbor’s kindness. Sit a while, or follow the road.”\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"woodland-elven-wayfarer\",\n  \"kind\": \"npc\",\n  \"region\": \"woodland\",\n  \"enemy\": \"elf\",\n  \"locations\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": [\n        65,\n        33\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"repeatable\": true,\n  \"accept\": [],\n  \"speech\": \"\\u201cThank you for the wick! Greenwood lies east. We\\u2019re fellow creatures under Christ, and glad of a neighbor\\u2019s kindness. Sit a while, or follow the road.\\u201d\",\n  \"grants\": []\n}\n```\n\n## reedbank-dockkeeper · Bram · The landing\n\nBram kneels beside a little boat, fitting a new oarlock. “Mind the rails. The current is lively this morning.” He points east along the boards. “Woodland Road is on this bank. No fare and no boat needed. Come back for the lantern race tonight.”\n\n#### Success\n\nThe morning carries on around you.\n\n#### Short\n\nBram kneels beside a little boat, fitting a new oarlock. “Mind the rails. The current is lively this morning.” He points east along the boards. “Woodland Road is on this bank. No fare and no boat needed. Come back for the lantern race tonight.”\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"reedbank-dockkeeper\",\n  \"kind\": \"npc\",\n  \"region\": \"riverbank\",\n  \"enemy\": \"boy\",\n  \"locations\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": [\n        32.3,\n        64.5\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"repeatable\": true,\n  \"accept\": [],\n  \"speech\": \"Bram kneels beside a little boat, fitting a new oarlock. \\u201cMind th\"\n}\n```\n\n## reedbank-leaf-race · Pella · Admiral of the leaf boats\n\n“That one is mine!” Pella points at a leaf disappearing below the landing. “It is carrying a very important ant.” She squints upstream. “I think.” The music starts again, and she skips back toward the cakes.\n\n#### Success\n\nThe morning carries on around you.\n\n#### Short\n\n“That one is mine!” Pella points at a leaf disappearing below the landing. “It is carrying a very important ant.” She squints upstream. “I think.” The music starts again, and she skips back toward the cakes.\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"reedbank-leaf-race\",\n  \"kind\": \"npc\",\n  \"region\": \"riverbank\",\n  \"enemy\": \"girl\",\n  \"locations\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": [\n        72,\n        56.1\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"repeatable\": true,\n  \"accept\": [],\n  \"speech\": \"\\u201cThat one is mine!\\u201d Pella points at a leaf disappearing below the\"\n}\n```\n\n## woodland-second-elf · Ithren · A guest at the fire\n\nIthren lifts a kettle from its hook. “There is room for one more cup.” His cloak is patched at both elbows. “I came looking for old inscriptions and found a leaking boot. The road is good at rearranging our plans.” He makes room beside the unlit fire ring. “We keep the fire small, and put it out before we leave.”\n\n#### Success\n\nThe morning carries on around you.\n\n#### Short\n\nIthren lifts a kettle from its hook. “There is room for one more cup.” His cloak is patched at both elbows. “I came looking for old inscriptions and found a leaking boot. The road is good at rearranging our plans.” He makes room beside the unlit fire ring. “We keep the fire small, and put it out before we leave.”\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"woodland-second-elf\",\n  \"kind\": \"npc\",\n  \"region\": \"woodland\",\n  \"enemy\": \"elf\",\n  \"locations\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": [\n        70.5,\n        28.8\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"repeatable\": true,\n  \"accept\": [],\n  \"speech\": \"Ithren lifts a kettle from its hook. \\u201cThere is room for one more \"\n}\n```\n\n";
